<urn:atm:triage:finding/FNX-010>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "FNX-010" ;
  triage:title "GateAfterTaskRead test double blocks a Tokio worker via std::sync::mpsc inside an async fn" ;
  triage:description "fenix's independent critical review of PR #1395 reports the GateAfterTaskRead test double (crates/atm-storage/src/testing.rs, load_logical_task) is properly registered in allowed_test_double_paths, but the gate calls std::sync::mpsc::Receiver::recv() inside async fn load_logical_task, blocking the calling Tokio worker until the test releases it. It works only because the one caller is #[tokio::test(flavor = \"multi_thread\", worker_threads = 2)] paired with spawn_blocking for the waiter (herdr_queue_wake.rs:1223,1294-1297). Any later use on a current-thread runtime, or with the gate held while the releasing task needs the same worker, deadlocks rather than failing -- the wrong primitive in a crate whose entire Async* companion family exists to keep blocking calls off Tokio tasks. Recommendation: use tokio::sync::oneshot/Notify for the gate, or document the multi-thread requirement on GateAfterTaskRead::new." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-az" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:category "test-infrastructure" ;
  triage:severity "minor" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
